{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_param_retired_1.march","start_line":4,"start_col":15,"end_line":4,"end_col":30,"message":"`greet` takes a `Cap(IO.Console)` parameter, but capability values were retired: a function no longer receives its authority, it uses the current authority, which `main`'s `needs` clause asks for and each operation checks.\nhelp: remove the parameter and the argument at each call; to state what `greet` may use, give it a `needs` clause.","code":"cap_param_retired","fix":{"kind":"multi","edits":[{"kind":"replace","start_line":4,"start_col":11,"end_line":4,"end_col":32,"text":""},{"kind":"replace","start_line":9,"start_col":10,"end_line":9,"end_col":13,"text":""}],"applicability":"machine-applicable"},"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
{"severity":"warning","file":"errors/cap_param_retired_1.march","start_line":8,"start_col":14,"end_line":8,"end_col":29,"message":"`main` asks for its authority with `Cap` parameters, which are deprecated and will be removed in the next release: a capability value grants nothing since the current authority replaced it.\nhelp: request it with a `needs` clause: `fn main() needs IO.Console do`.","code":"deprecated_main_cap","fix":{"kind":"multi","edits":[{"kind":"replace","start_line":8,"start_col":9,"end_line":8,"end_col":30,"text":"()"},{"kind":"replace","start_line":8,"start_col":31,"end_line":8,"end_col":31,"text":"needs IO.Console "}],"applicability":"machine-applicable"},"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
